OL,3,AGhana's new $60m presidential jet
OL,4,Asparks public outrage
OL,5,
OL,6,FGhana's government has defended its
OL,7,Fpurchase of a new presidential jet amid
OL,8,Fcriticism over its cost, as many
OL,9,Fcitizens continue to struggle with the
OL,10,Fhigh cost of living.
OL,12,FThe $60m (#46m) French-made Falcon 6X
OL,13,Fhas sparked a political row, with
OL,14,Fopposition politicians accusing
OL,15,FPresident John Mahama's administration
OL,16,Fof misplaced priorities.
OL,18,FBut the government says the purchase is
OL,19,Fjustified, arguing that Ghana's
OL,20,Fimproving economy makes the aircraft
OL,21,Faffordable and is needed to replace an
OL,22,Fageing presidential jet.
OL,23,APub: 18-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
